> Thus, at a bare minimum, Vlad himself needs to be improved upon;

I tend to agree.  I can see arguments to the contrary (e.g.,
having him be an utter wuss is arguably kind of humorous,
particularly for Castlevania players, and that's probably
why the devs did him that way -- it was almost certainly
deliberate), but I don't find such arguments very compelling,
personally.

> his Tower could possibly use some changes as well

I suppose, but at a lower priority than Gehennom; it's
a relatively small area and not very boring, really.

> Indeed, most variants I'm aware of buff Vlad considerably
> in some fashion

I know SporkHack does, and you mentioned doing so in GruntHack.
I also seem to recall seeing something about Vlad related to
UnNetHack.  And yes, when multiple variants independently do
something, there's often some kind of reason.

